# FMT-A regression fixture (Round XXXVI): the `Expr::UnaryOp` arm's
# `not` variant parses operand at bp 20, distinct from `-`/`~` which
# parse at bp 33. `not (a and b)` re-emits as `not a and b` = `Not(a) and b`
# instead of `Not(and(a,b))` without the paren wrap.
#
# The helper's per-op `prefix_bp` parameter (20 for `not`, 33 for others)
# ensures the right wrap decision is made.
#
# Pre-fix RED signature: `gg fmt` re-emitted `bool r = not a and b`
# and running the reformatted file printed `false` instead of `true`.
void main():
    bool a = true
    bool b = false
    bool r = not (a and b)
    print(r)
